# aurora.local / packages/monitoring/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/monitoring/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/monitoring/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# prom/prometheus — latest stable is v3.13.2 (2026-07-29), a security
# patch (bumps golang.org/x/text for CVE-2026-56852). There is a
# v3.14.0-rc.0 out (2026-08-06) — deliberately skipped, it's a release
# candidate. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64,
# linux/ppc64le, linux/riscv64, linux/s390x — confirmed. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_PROMETHEUS=prom/prometheus:v3.13.2@sha256:508729e0e2d18e11fd742a5a5ca70e557b940a93948c3c95fd0123a6fd538b69

# grafana/grafana — latest OSS release is 13.1.3 (2026-08-07, 8 days
# before this check — fresh, but not a beta/rc; Grafana ships patch
# releases on odd months by design). Note compose.yml uses
# `grafana/grafana`, not `grafana/grafana-oss` — the plain `grafana/grafana`
# image runs the OSS feature set without a licence key, so this pin
# keeps the same image, just names the version. Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_GRAFANA=grafana/grafana:13.1.3@sha256:ab5cb380e3ff3172d6c8bd2e7cfd31cce977d2881b260e1f5bc089bf0b759b43

# prom/node-exporter — latest stable is v1.12.1 (2026-07-14). Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64, linux/ppc64le, linux/riscv64,
# linux/s390x — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_NODE_EXPORTER=prom/node-exporter:v1.12.1@sha256:1b4e4438faca4dd7e001dd445d161a4a2091b0fededa84093b3a8dfeae1f1be0

# gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor — FINDING: this registry path is deprecated.
# cAdvisor moved its published images to ghcr.io/google/cadvisor as of
# v0.53.0 and the project's own docs say so. Verified directly: gcr.io
# only serves up to v0.55.1 (`:latest` there resolves to exactly
# v0.55.1, and v0.56.2/v0.60.4/v0.60.5 all 404 on gcr.io), while
# ghcr.io/google/cadvisor is current at v0.60.5. compose.yml still
# points at the old gcr.io path, so — staying within that same image
# name — the honest pin is v0.55.1, five-plus minor releases stale, not
# a currently-updating "safe" pin in the way the other images in this
# file are. Recorded for reference only (NOT adopted, since it's a
# different image and out of scope for this task):
#   ghcr.io/google/cadvisor:v0.60.5@sha256:763aecf1c32c2be8a1a75f9abfc2fc461005c9dbbaa39cb356b354aac1296dbe
# Multi-arch on gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor: linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7,
# linux/arm64, linux/s390x — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_CADVISOR=gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:v0.55.1@sha256:3de2bd5203120b866d74a9b283b2ffb8ec382fbf9dc321814700c6ea6f44ec57

# louislam/uptime-kuma — compose.yml pins the floating major tag `:1`.
# FINDING: Uptime Kuma has moved to a 2.x line (2.5.0 is the current
# actively-developed release as of this check) — 1.x is no longer where
# new development happens. The last-ever 1.x release is 1.23.17, pushed
# ~10 months before this check (`:1` already resolves to exactly this).
# Per this task's guidance on breaking major bumps: pinned to the
# current major (1.23.17) rather than jumping to 2.x, since a monitor
# config/DB migration across a major version is a deliberate decision
# for the owner, not a routine pin — but note 1.x will not receive
# further updates either, so this is a stable stopping point, not an
# indefinitely safe one. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7,
# linux/arm64 — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_UPTIME_KUMA=louislam/uptime-kuma:1.23.17@sha256:3d632903e6af34139a37f18055c4f1bfd9b7205ae1138f1e5e8940ddc1d176f9
